{
  "id": "empty-a-session-that-handed-on",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "THE OTHER HALF OF THE HANDOVER, AND THE ONLY DESTRUCTIVE THING THE RELAY DOES. When a session of this machine finishes a turn, this flow asks two questions, and empties nothing unless both answer. First the session's own context: the reading must stand at oblige, taken from the transcript the command line writes about itself, not from stillness and not from the age of a mandate. Second the store: has the terminal that just spoke left a mandate nobody has taken? If either answers no the flow ends green with nothing done. **A MANDATE ON DISK IS NOT CONSENT.** On 11/09/2026 this flow, keyed on the mandate alone, emptied a session that had written its handover seventeen minutes earlier and had gone on working, and a person lost the thread of an investigation in progress. Depositing a handover is something a session is asked to do while it keeps working; it is not a statement that it is finished. A session standing at oblige is. If both answer yes, the session is emptied by the line that command line's own descriptor declares, and only once the emptying has asked everything again itself, together, at the moment it types, because a run can park for hours and a terminal is reused: the session in the terminal now must be the one that left the mandate, the mandate must still be untaken, that session's own context must stand at oblige now, and the reading must say nobody is being waited for in there: the screen has stood still for as long as the line declares, its prompt is painted, and none of the marks that mean a person is being asked something is on it. In every other case the answer is «not yet» and nothing is typed. The name of the command line is read from the mandate itself, so no product is named in this file. The mandate the successor then reads arrives with the greeting of its own session. **A GREETING NOBODY ANSWERS IS NOT A HANDOVER.** That greeting is context, not a turn: the session opened by the emptying was handed its mandate and then stood at the prompt until a person typed a word, so every relay ended with the work waiting on somebody. The flow therefore does not end at the emptying. It waits for the successor to say it is there — the store says so, and only the store: the mandate marked taken by a name that is not its author's — and then, once the reading says the new session is standing at a painted prompt and nobody is being waited for in there, types one line to start it. If nobody takes it inside the time written here, the answer is «not yet» and nothing else is typed: a line into a terminal where no successor arrived would land in whatever is standing there.",
